---
description: Never expose secrets or personal data in code, logs, commits, PRs, or reusable notes
globs:
alwaysApply: true
---

- Never print, paste, or commit secret values (API keys, tokens, passwords, OAuth client secrets, cookies). Reference them by variable name only (`process.env.OPENROUTER_API_KEY`, `${env:NAME}`).
- Do not read secret files just to echo or copy them; if a value is missing, report which variable is missing.
- Personal data (government ID numbers, home addresses, phone numbers, real names in records): minimise and redact in summaries, fixtures, logs, test data, and any reusable memory/notes unless the immediate task strictly requires the exact value.
- Test fixtures and seed data use obviously fake values.
- High-risk actions — real money, real outbound messages, bypassing captchas/verification, CDP injection, process-memory reads — are out of scope unless the task explicitly requests them; stop and report instead.
